    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590">

                <pb facs="0574" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1978½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <p>After conference with the President on Saturday, June 1, it was agreed that I
                    should say to Lord Reading that this Government was entirely willing to send
                    troops to Murmansk provided General <pb facs="0575" n="485" xml:id="pg485"/>
                    Foch approved the diversion of troops and the necessary shipping for that
                    purpose from those now going to France. Before doing this I saw Secretary Baker
                    who entirely agreed with this action and to-day I saw Lord Reading and told him
                    of our attitude. He made notes and said he would inform his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>
                    <lb/><dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                                1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1918.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
